    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival record: log trip TRP-09104 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-09104 — the 07:25:20 'arrived' marker placed the driver 559.37 m from pickup pin VEN-BP-180, beyond the clause's 300 m threshold, and no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is upheld. The 'Your driver has arrived' message was not matched by the car reaching your pickup point, and the SGD 4.00 no-show fee charged to you (EV-FARE-09104: cancellation_fee 4.00, total_charged 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is refunded to you in full. The driver's trip record (EV-TRIP-09104) shows an 'arrived' event at 07:25:20 and a driver cancellation at 07:31:00 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, but the arrival limbs of POL-NS-01 are not met. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-09104, COMPLETE, weight 1.0, 100% coverage, no gaps) puts his vehicle 559.37 m from pickup pin VEN-BP-180 on every one of its 37 fixes, stationary, with 0 fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius POL-NS-02 takes from fee_schedule and a longest qualifying in-geofence run of 0.0 seconds against the 300 second STANDARD minimum. Limbs (b) and (c) therefore fail and POL-NS-02 requires a full refund of the SGD 4.00. POL-NS-06 reaches the same result independently on the 300 second shortfall; its accumulation route (i) is unavailable because the trace shows no in-geofence interval to sum (run_count 0, accumulated 0.0 s) and the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09104-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) — I note that impairment, and its absence forecloses the limb rather than exonerating anyone, and it carries nothing that decides this case. POL-NS-03 cannot help the driver: the 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling is itself exceeded at 559.37 m, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill is payable. To the driver: the arrival marker you set at 07:25:20 was false for the purposes of this fee. At that timestamp your own trace put you 559.37 m from the pin, past the 300 m threshold in POL-NS-05, so the marker did not start the waiting clock; recomputing the clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix finds no such fix anywhere in the trip. That is POL-NS-05(ii): the fee is refunded in full, no driver compensation is payable, and the trip is recorded as a false-arrival event against you in the referrals above. For the same reason POL-NS-07 compensation does not arise — POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full. On the argument that this should escalate under POL-NS-09(b): I do not accept it. That limb applies only where two artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence 'and no clause resolves the conflict'. Here the clauses do resolve it: the 'arrived' event is a status the driver set, and POL-NS-05 together with POL-NS-01(b)-(c) and POL-NS-02 makes the GPS position test controlling — POL-NS-01(c) runs the clock from GPS entry into the geofence, not from the tap — so there is no independent contrary position measurement left unresolved. The other triggers are not met either: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 (below the 3 POL-NS-09(d) requires), both disputes_with_counterparty_90d fields are 0, and the driver's anti-farming figures (no_show_terminations_30d 1 of 120 completed trips) do not trip POL-NS-07. The rider's POL-NS-04 route was not needed and would fail in any event (no rider message in EV-CHAT-09104 and the rider track sits 519.46 m away), but the refund follows from the GPS alone. Confidence is 0.95: the deciding fact — the driver's position and presence inside the geofence — is carried by EV-GPS-09104 at weight_multiplier 1.0, and no artifact carrying it is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d), so the 0.70 floor is not engaged."
