    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your dispute succeeds in full and the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is returned to you. To the driver: the fee your arrival marker produced cannot stand, and no compensation is payable to you.\n\nWhy the SGD 4.00 is not chargeable. POL-NS-01 charges a no-show fee only where all four of its conditions hold. Limb (a) holds — EV-TRIP-09104 carries an 'arrived' event at 07:25:20 — and limb (d) holds — no boarding (started_at null) and the trip terminated by the driver at 07:31:00 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW. Limbs (b) and (c) fail on the driver's own trace, EV-GPS-09104 (weight 1.0, COMPLETE). All 37 driver fixes sit 559.37 m from the pickup pin (min_distance_m = mean_distance_m = max_distance_m = 559.3707 m), the derived arrival block reports qualifying_fix_count 0, and the longest continuous in-geofence run is 0.0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum. POL-NS-02 therefore applies with full force: with no qualifying in-radius fix at any point in the 15 minutes before the 07:31:00 cancellation, the driver is not deemed to have arrived, limb (b) fails, and the rider is entitled to a full refund. EV-FARE-09104 (weight 1.0) itemises the fee at SGD 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so SGD 4.00 is the sum returned.\n\nPOL-NS-05 makes the same finding at the marker itself. At the 07:25:20 'arrived' timestamp the trace places the driver 559.37 m from the pin, far beyond the clause's 300 m threshold, so the marker is FALSE and starts no waiting clock. Recomputed from the first qualifying in-geofence fix there is none (qualifying_fix_count 0), which is POL-NS-05(ii): the fee is refunded in full, no compensation is payable, and the trip is recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver — that instruction is carried in the referrals list.\n\nPOL-NS-03 does not rescue the charge. Its entire test is that the driver held position not more than 400 m from the pickup pin; the stationary fixes sit at 559.37 m, outside that ceiling, so the wrong-entrance route and any pin-ambiguity goodwill under POL-NS-03(ii) are unavailable. POL-NS-06 confirms the refund independently: the effective in-geofence dwell is 0.0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, a 300-second shortfall, and the clause refunds in full whether or not the rider was present or responsive. POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is not open — run_count 0 leaves no second in-geofence interval to sum, and EV-ADVIS-09104-01 is MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0, disclosed here), so no present and populated traffic advisory exists and nothing may be asserted against it.\n\nThe driver's argument for holding the SGD 4.00 under POL-NS-09(b) is rejected. That trigger requires two admissible artifacts to contradict each other on arrival 'and no clause resolves the conflict'. POL-NS-05 is the clause written for exactly this conflict: it makes the GPS position authoritative over the arrival marker, and POL-NS-02 independently decides the geofence question. The system notice 'Your driver has arrived' in EV-CHAT-09104 is the platform's broadcast of the driver's own marker, not an independent account of the driver's position, and the driver's own statement concedes he merely 'marked arrival and waited'. No other POL-NS-09 trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; no artifact carrying the deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d) (20-second marker/fix skew, no trace gap, 37 fixes, chat count matching trip_record.chat_message_count, fee reconciling at SGD 4.00 under the resolution rule); rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and both counterparty-dispute counters are 0; and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1 is below 4, and 1/120 = 0.008 is below 0.08).\n\nClaims dealt with. The rider's limbs (b) and (c) failures, the POL-NS-02 full-refund claim, the POL-NS-05 false-marker claim, the POL-NS-06 shortfall claim, the POL-NS-03 unavailability claim, the POL-NS-06(i) unavailability claim and the claim that no POL-NS-09 trigger is met are all accepted and together produce the refund. The driver's claims that SGD 4.00 is the correct amount (STANDARD zone-class fee SGD 4.00, RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee SGD 4.00, GREATER taken, no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect), that limbs (a) and (d) hold, that POL-NS-04 cannot run (no rider message in EV-CHAT-09104 and rider_qualifying_fix_count 0 at 519.46 m), and the driver's express concession that the fee is not chargeable on the GPS record are accepted; the first four do not change the outcome and the concession corroborates it. No driver compensation is payable, because POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied in full and it is not. Every artifact the ruling rests on carries weight 1.0, so the confidence cap under POL-GEN-02(2) is 1.0 and confidence is set at 0.95."
  },
